# Spotify Web API app credentials (Authorization Code + PKCE — no client
# secret needed, and NONE should ever be put in this file or shipped to the
# browser: this is a fully static/client-side app, so anything here ends up
# readable in the deployed JS bundle).
#
# Create an app at https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard, then under
# Edit Settings -> Redirect URIs add BOTH of these (Spotify lets an app
# register several):
#   http://127.0.0.1:3000/callback   (local dev — NOT "localhost": Spotify
#                                      rejects that hostname literal)
#   https://www.musiquee.pl/callback (production)
#
# Leave both vars below empty to run Musiquee fully in Demo Mode (no
# Spotify account required).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=

# Optional: pin the redirect_uri explicitly instead of letting the app infer
# it from window.location.origin. Required in production if that origin
# ever differs from the registered URI; for local dev you can usually leave
# this unset and the app will self-correct "localhost" to "127.0.0.1".
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SPOTIFY_REDIRECT_URI=http://127.0.0.1:3000/callback
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SPOTIFY_REDIRECT_URI=https://www.musiquee.pl/callback
